# s6: daemon revocation destroys the sprite   (UTC 2026-09-17)

The Daemons page revokes through the TanStack server function `revokeDaemon` (src/daemons/functions.ts:153),
which calls operations.handleOrganizationDaemonRevocation -> DaemonRegistration.revoke
(src/daemons/registration.ts:68), which does database.revokeDaemon(id) then activeDaemons.revoke(daemon).
src/app.ts:443 wires registry.onRevoked to
lifecycle.failPendingExecutionsForDisconnectedMachine(daemon.machineId, "daemon_revoked"), and that is the
function this PR changed to destroy the sprite.

It was driven through the real page, not a synthetic call. Two cheaper routes were tried first and are
recorded because they are not reproducible shortcuts:
  - POST /_serverFn/5032765fc5ca881367c43f47f2c31cdaa723f36bc12b02504a04c33386498ffb with a session cookie
    and a plain JSON body: 403 "Forbidden" through the tunnel (TanStack's same-origin referer guard sees
    the request origin as http://127.0.0.1:3001, not the tunnel host), and 500 with a seroval decode error
    when posted to 127.0.0.1:3001, because the RPC body is not plain JSON. No daemon was revoked by either.
  - There is no public-API route for revocation; `/organization/daemons/revoke` exists only behind the
    server function.

## Through the dashboard

Sign in as the bootstrap owner -> forced "Choose a new password" (ac-vni finding 6 again) -> "Set up your
apps" -> "Do this later" -> /o/qa-ac50k-e2f1be93/daemons.

The Daemons table listed five rows for this trigger, slugs `trigger-<triggerId>` for the first daemon and
`trigger-<triggerId>-<daemonId[0:8]>` for every later one (ac-vni finding 4 / ac-52w finding 13, unchanged).
Row 450d02b3 read Status "Offline", Access "Hub automations".

Actions -> Revoke -> "Revoke trigger-…-450d02b3? The daemon will disconnect and its credential cannot
reconnect." -> Revoke daemon.

